Subject: Allocate the AOT assumption cells, deopt counters and disable bits per runtime

What this does
  The unit declares how many assumption cells, guard sites and functions it has;
  each runtime allocates its own arrays of those sizes at first use. The engine
  gains `qjs_aot_cells`, `qjs_aot_func_disabled` and `qjs_aot_note_deopt`, and
  the run state is freed with the runtime.

Why we need it
  Shapes, prototypes and globals belong to one runtime, and a process can run
  several on different threads, so a cell or counter in the unit's static data
  would be unsound and racy: registered against runtime A's objects it would
  never fire when runtime B changes its own. The unit therefore declares the
  layout and the runtime owns the data (§5.6, §6.5).

What it adds
  `JSAotRun` (cells, deopt hits, disable bits, the K limit), `aot_run_ensure`/
  `aot_run_free`, the accessors above, `qjs_aot_cell_count`/`qjs_aot_site_count`
  as unit symbols, and `cells=`/`disabled=` in the `QJS_AOT_STATS` line.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

